WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.868 --> 00:00:02.000
-You look fantastic.

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:03.634
Juno, thank you so much
for being here.

00:00:03.634 --> 00:00:05.501
-Thank you for having me.
I'm so excited.

00:00:05.501 --> 00:00:07.100
I can't believe this
is all real.

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:08.834
-We have so much to talk about.
-Mm-hmm.

00:00:08.834 --> 00:00:10.167
-First off, I want to talk about
"The Offer."

00:00:10.167 --> 00:00:12.100
This is on Paramount+.

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:15.467
This is the story of how
"The Godfather" got made.

00:00:15.467 --> 00:00:18.367
I didn't know any of
these stories going into it.

00:00:18.367 --> 00:00:19.634
Did you?
-No, neither did I.

00:00:19.634 --> 00:00:20.834
I knew nothing.

00:00:20.834 --> 00:00:23.334
Like, the fact that
the amount of hurdles,

00:00:23.334 --> 00:00:26.133
the amount of complications,
the amount of [bleep]...

00:00:26.133 --> 00:00:27.267
-Yes. Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:00:27.267 --> 00:00:28.567
-...that was thrown
at everybody.

00:00:28.567 --> 00:00:30.133
-Even if you whisper it,
you still can't say it.

00:00:30.133 --> 00:00:31.300
Yeah, it's interesting.

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:35.467
-Of shindigs that were
thrown at the production

00:00:35.467 --> 00:00:38.734
that ultimately created one of
the greatest films of all time

00:00:38.734 --> 00:00:41.667
was something that, yeah,
I really knew nothing about.

00:00:41.667 --> 00:00:44.067
-Yeah. I, like --
I didn't know that --

00:00:44.067 --> 00:00:45.334
I didn't know how
important your --

00:00:45.334 --> 00:00:48.067
-They didn't want
Francis Ford Coppola, yes?

00:00:48.067 --> 00:00:50.067
-They didn't want Francis Ford
or Marlon Brando.

00:00:50.067 --> 00:00:52.667
-No.
And Al Pacino almost got fired.

00:00:52.667 --> 00:00:54.434
These are all the people
that I --

00:00:54.434 --> 00:00:56.601
They make me want to do
this job, you know?

00:00:56.601 --> 00:00:58.267
-Isn't that wild?
-Yeah, it was crazy.

00:00:58.267 --> 00:01:00.067
-If you think about --
You never know what goes into

00:01:00.067 --> 00:01:01.567
what and how much work goes
into everything.

00:01:01.567 --> 00:01:02.868
Like, that's "The Godfather."

00:01:02.868 --> 00:01:05.200
-And the time and the passion
and the persistence

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.167
and that Al Ruddy, played by the
extraordinary Miles Teller --

00:01:08.167 --> 00:01:10.000
-Yeah, he's great.
-Just -- Yeah.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:11.868
[ Cheers and applause ]
I love him. I love him.

00:01:11.868 --> 00:01:13.567
-Now, you two together, come on.

00:01:13.567 --> 00:01:15.167
Can we just even
talk about "Ted Lasso"

00:01:15.167 --> 00:01:16.400
for a second, please?

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:18.234
-Yeah.
-Congratulations.

00:01:18.234 --> 00:01:21.467
It is a global --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:21.467 --> 00:01:23.367
Second Emmy nomination for you.

00:01:23.367 --> 00:01:25.334
-It's so crazy.
-Yeah.

00:01:25.334 --> 00:01:27.000
What was it like,
the first Emmys?

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:28.767
Did you go, "Oh,
wow, this is a big deal" or

00:01:28.767 --> 00:01:29.934
"People are starting to watch"?

00:01:29.934 --> 00:01:31.067
-It was so surreal.

00:01:31.067 --> 00:01:32.501
It was -- I think you never --

00:01:32.501 --> 00:01:34.567
can ever guess that anything
like that would happen.

00:01:34.567 --> 00:01:37.968
And then the fact that the show
got nominated a lot of times

00:01:37.968 --> 00:01:40.634
last round of Emmys
and that I got to go with

00:01:40.634 --> 00:01:43.200
Hannah Waddingham,
who is one of my best friends

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:44.267
in the entire world.

00:01:44.267 --> 00:01:45.300
-She is amazing.

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:46.701
By the way, she can sing,
by the way.

00:01:46.701 --> 00:01:48.767
-She can sing. She can dance.
She can cuddle.

00:01:48.767 --> 00:01:51.033
She can make you laugh.
She can make you cry.

00:01:51.033 --> 00:01:53.467
She's got -- I love to just
lay in her chest.

00:01:53.467 --> 00:01:55.501
-Yeah. That's so funny.
-Yeah

00:01:55.501 --> 00:01:57.734
And we -- I waited for her,
because she --

00:01:57.734 --> 00:01:58.801
We arrived at different times.

00:01:58.801 --> 00:02:00.767
And when we walked
into the room,

00:02:00.767 --> 00:02:02.667
our category was up first.

00:02:02.667 --> 00:02:06.400
And I kid you not, she
literately sat and went, "Up!"

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:07.400
And I was like,
"You've got to go up.

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:08.667
Don't sit. Go, go."

00:02:08.667 --> 00:02:10.868
And it was this immediate --
And then her speech.

00:02:10.868 --> 00:02:12.033
-That was great.

00:02:12.033 --> 00:02:14.434
Aww! You got such a good ca--

00:02:14.434 --> 00:02:16.400
I mean, did you --
Backstage, you were saying,

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:18.133
"Yeah, I didn't know if
I could be funny

00:02:18.133 --> 00:02:21.167
or I didn't think that --"
Like, you're a dramatic actor.

00:02:21.167 --> 00:02:22.667
-I was known definitely
more for --

00:02:22.667 --> 00:02:26.200
Yes, you know, I've played,
like, lesbian werewolves.

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:27.400
I've played --
-That will get you typecast.

00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:28.901
Yeah.

00:02:28.901 --> 00:02:31.033
-Yeah. Well, I've spent quite
a lot of time in trailer parks,

00:02:31.033 --> 00:02:32.734
too, you know,
going through some [bleep]

00:02:32.734 --> 00:02:33.834
-Yeah.
-Some stuff.

00:02:33.834 --> 00:02:35.734
-Whisper it.
-Going through some stuff.

00:02:35.734 --> 00:02:37.667
-Please, whisper it.
Thank you.

00:02:37.667 --> 00:02:41.033
Please, just if you're going to
say it, whisper it, yeah.

00:02:41.033 --> 00:02:42.968
It goes right under the censors.
They don't even know.

00:02:42.968 --> 00:02:44.834
-Whoo!
-But who cast you?

00:02:44.834 --> 00:02:47.033
Jason Sudeikis?
-Well, he sent me a text.

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:48.968
And there was this moment where
I thought, "Oh, gosh.

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:50.334
This is going to be awkward,

00:02:50.334 --> 00:02:54.067
because I'm pretty sure
he has text the wrong actress.

00:02:54.067 --> 00:02:55.567
And I'm going to have to write
back and be like,

00:02:55.567 --> 00:02:57.801
"Yo, this is Juno Temple.

00:02:57.801 --> 00:03:00.133
I don't know if you
actually know who I am."

00:03:00.133 --> 00:03:03.067
-Yeah. You sent the wrong text,
but it sounds like a great part.

00:03:03.067 --> 00:03:04.534
-Yeah, I'm super into
reading it.

00:03:04.534 --> 00:03:06.033
Yeah, yeah. Let's definitely
talk about it later.

00:03:06.033 --> 00:03:07.300
And it wasn't a mistake.

00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:10.167
And I think that, you know,
he has this ability

00:03:10.167 --> 00:03:12.067
with a lot of people
that were cast in the show

00:03:12.067 --> 00:03:13.834
to see something
in all of us that we didn't

00:03:13.834 --> 00:03:16.701
necessarily think
we had in us at all.

00:03:16.701 --> 00:03:19.167
That being said,
a lot of the times,

00:03:19.167 --> 00:03:21.601
I'm telling jokes on
"Ted Lasso."

00:03:21.601 --> 00:03:24.267
I don't know
they're a joke, so...

00:03:24.267 --> 00:03:26.601
-Well, good.
That adds to the mystique.

00:03:26.601 --> 00:03:27.934
-Definitely.
-Yeah.

00:03:27.934 --> 00:03:29.834
-And also because we get a lot
of ever-changing dialogue

00:03:29.834 --> 00:03:32.200
and the fluidity of kind of
keeping our brains working

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:33.367
and things like that.

00:03:33.367 --> 00:03:35.434
Because Jason comes from
the world that you do,

00:03:35.434 --> 00:03:37.601
of "Saturday Night Live,"
where you guys are very quick at

00:03:37.601 --> 00:03:40.033
learning anything that is
handed in front of you,

00:03:40.033 --> 00:03:44.167
where I am used to sticky-tab
every single sentence

00:03:44.167 --> 00:03:45.501
I'm going to say,
and I highlight it with

00:03:45.501 --> 00:03:47.334
matching highlighters
to the sticky tab,

00:03:47.334 --> 00:03:49.601
which tells me
what day I'm shooting, when,

00:03:49.601 --> 00:03:52.367
where my character's at,
where it was two weeks ago.

00:03:52.367 --> 00:03:53.501
It's a whole thing.

00:03:53.501 --> 00:03:56.501
-No, all we do is
look at the cue cards.

00:03:57.767 --> 00:04:00.534
It's all written over there.

00:04:00.534 --> 00:04:02.834
You've got to get cue cards.
-Do you have some?

00:04:02.834 --> 00:04:03.901
-You have to get
cue cards, yeah.

00:04:03.901 --> 00:04:05.067
-Can I take some?

00:04:05.067 --> 00:04:07.734
-Juno, do you understand --
Like, do you feel

00:04:07.734 --> 00:04:09.968
what you've done and what you're
doing for the world?

00:04:09.968 --> 00:04:12.400
Because people love you.
I hope you know this.

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:15.133
Like, do people tell
you how much they love you?

00:04:15.133 --> 00:04:16.834
You're a part of their world.

00:04:16.834 --> 00:04:18.267
Do people come up
to you and say,

00:04:18.267 --> 00:04:21.033
"Hey, thank you" or "I love you"
or "You make me laugh"

00:04:21.033 --> 00:04:22.367
or anything?

00:04:22.367 --> 00:04:25.200
-Yeah. You know what?
Sometimes, they do, actually.

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:27.367
And that's something that I --
With this show,

00:04:27.367 --> 00:04:30.434
it feels so special because you
get to go, "I'm a fan, too."

00:04:30.434 --> 00:04:31.934
I love being a part of the show.

00:04:31.934 --> 00:04:33.033
But there was
this beautiful moment.

00:04:33.033 --> 00:04:34.968
Me and Hannah
were doing press for --

00:04:34.968 --> 00:04:37.467
it was for Season 2 --
when we were filming Season 2,

00:04:37.467 --> 00:04:38.567
so a lot of it was on Zoom.

00:04:38.567 --> 00:04:40.200
And we were doing a Zoom thing.

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:42.501
And this lovely woman
was interviewing us,

00:04:42.501 --> 00:04:45.701
and she just said to us both
that she was proud to show

00:04:45.701 --> 00:04:47.634
this show to her daughter
when she grew up

00:04:47.634 --> 00:04:50.734
because it was so important to
see two women who really

00:04:50.734 --> 00:04:53.167
actually are best friends
and who root for each other

00:04:53.167 --> 00:04:56.834
in a way that is genuinely about
seeing the other one

00:04:56.834 --> 00:04:58.434
blossom and be the best
that they can be

00:04:58.434 --> 00:04:59.634
and support each other,

00:04:59.634 --> 00:05:02.267
but also call each other out
when necessary.

00:05:02.267 --> 00:05:05.501
Your girlfriends are
so important.

00:05:05.501 --> 00:05:06.634
-I want to show a clip.

00:05:06.634 --> 00:05:08.834
Here's Juno Temple in
"Ted Lasso."

00:05:08.834 --> 00:05:10.234
Take a look at this.

00:05:10.234 --> 00:05:12.501
-That baby sucks.

00:05:12.501 --> 00:05:14.501
-You don't have to
say that to me.

00:05:14.501 --> 00:05:16.133
-I'm not just saying it.
I'm serious.

00:05:16.133 --> 00:05:18.100
That baby's whack.

00:05:18.100 --> 00:05:20.601
I hate it.

00:05:20.601 --> 00:05:24.133
-I love you.
-I love you, too.

00:05:24.133 --> 00:05:25.467
I'm here for you,
whatever you need.

00:05:25.467 --> 00:05:26.834
-I know.

00:05:26.834 --> 00:05:29.234
-I won't leave your side.

00:05:29.234 --> 00:05:30.234
-Jones!

00:05:30.234 --> 00:05:32.868
-Sassy! Oh, my God!

00:05:33.968 --> 00:05:36.934
Oh! Hi!

00:05:36.934 --> 00:05:40.267
-There you go right there.
Juno Temple, everyone.

00:05:40.267 --> 00:05:43.000
"Ted Lasso" is on Apple TV+.

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:45.367
Check out "The Offer"
on Paramount+.

00:05:45.367 --> 00:05:48.167
We'll be right back with a
performance from Demi Lovato.

00:05:48.167 --> 00:05:49.801
Stick around, everybody.
Come on back.

